%[text] %[text:anchor:T_AB5F32C3] # Solving the Reissner-Mindlin plate problem using sparse matrices and page-wise implementation
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] In this appendix it is demonstrated how to leverage [`sparse`](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/sparse.html)-matrices and [page-wise operations](https://blogs.mathworks.com/loren/2021/01/14/paged-matrix-functions/) in [MATLAB](https://www.mathworks.com/products/matlab.html)® to speed-up the computation, assembly and solution of the linear equation systems resulting from the discretization of the [Reissner-Mindlin plate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mindlin%E2%80%93Reissner_plate_theory) *Boundary Value Problem* (BVP).
%[text] 
%[text] **Author: Andreas Apostolatos, PhD (aapostol@mathworks.com)**
%[text] **Date: 20.02.2023**
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF2E5D07] ## Preamble
clc;
clear;
close all;
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_F78170C0] ## **Problem parameters**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B5E52518] ### Geometric parameters
%[text] Plate's thickness \[m\]
propStr.t = 10^(-1); %[control:slider:6356]{"position":[17,19]} %[text:anchor:M_08BBF242]
%[text] X-coordinate of left corner \[m\]
X0 = 0;
%[text] X-coordinate of right corner \[m\]
XLx = 4;
%[text] Y-coordinate of left corner \[m\]
Y0 = 0;
%[text] Y-coordinate of right corner \[m\]
YLy = 1;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_FD0F76EA] ### Material paramerters
%[text] Distributed load \[N/m^2\]
propStr.pBar = -1e2;
%[text] Distributed moment around x-axis \[N/m\]
propStr.mxBar = 0;
%[text] Distributed moment around y-axis \[N/m\]
propStr.myBar = 0;
%[text] Young's modulus \[N/m^2\]
propStr.E = 1e7;
%[text] Poisson ratio \[dimensionless\]
propStr.nu = 0;
%[text] Shear modulus (connected to epsilon\_12 = E/(1+nu)) \[N/m^2\]
propStr.G = propStr.E/2/(1 + propStr.nu);
%[text] Plate's stiffness \[Nm\]
propStr.D = propStr.E*propStr.t^3/12/(1 - propStr.nu^2);
%[text] Shear-correction factor
propStr.alpha = 5/6;
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_518CB8A7] ## Analytical solution using the Timoshenko beam formulation
%[text] Since the plate is rectangular, clamped on its one end while being subject to constant distributed vertical load its behavior is expected to resemble a beam aligned with the X-axis, whereas no effects are expected to take place along the Y-axis. The analytical solution for this problem using the shear-deformable Timoshenko beam formulation are in this case as follows
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B05D0DF2] ### Initialize auxiliary variables
syms wEx(X) betayEx(X) qxEx(X) Lsym psym Gsym Aqsym Esym Isym tsym alphaScf
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E243EEEE] ### Analytical solution with respect to the vertical deflection
%[text] Set the analytical solution in terms of the vertical deflection field (Eq. (1) in the introduction):
%[text] $w(X,Y) = \\frac{1}{\\alpha G A} \\left( \\overline{p} L X - \\frac{\\overline{p} X^2}{2} \\right) - \\frac{1}{EI} \\left( - \\frac{\\overline{p} X^4}{24} + \\frac{\\overline{p} L X^3}{6} - \\frac{\\overline{p} L^2 X^2}{4} \\right) \\qquad (3)$
%[text] namely:
wEx(X) = (psym*Lsym*X-psym*X^2/2)/Gsym/(Aqsym) - ...
    (-psym*X^4/24+psym*Lsym*X^3/6-psym*Lsym^2*X^2/4)/Esym/Isym;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51569EC4] ### Analytical solution with respect to the transverse-shear forces
%[text] Get the analytical solution of the rotational field by leveraging the Partial Differential Equation (PDE) of the problem and the functions of the [Symbolic Math Toolbox](https://www.mathworks.com/products/symbolic.html)™ in [MATLAB](https://www.mathworks.com/products/matlab.html)®
%[text] $\\beta(X,y) = \\int\_{0}^L - \\frac{1}{\\alpha G A}\\overline{p} - \\frac{\\partial^2 w}{\\partial x^2} \\: \\text{d}x  \\qquad (4)$
betayEx(X) = int(-1/(propStr.alpha*propStr.G*YLy*propStr.t)*propStr.pBar - ...
    diff(diff(wEx, X), X));
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_4FF8DB3D] ### Analytical solution with respect to the transverse-shear forces
%[text] Herein we are concerned with the resultant transverse-shear force component $q\_x(X,Y) = \\alpha G t \\gamma\_x = \\alpha G t \\overbrace{\\left( \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial X} + \\beta\_y \\right)}^{\\gamma\_x}$ because $q\_y(X,Y)$ is identically zero across the plate due to the given setup. Resultant transverse-shear force component $q\_x(X,Y) $ is given by:
qxEx(X) = alphaScf*Gsym*tsym*(diff(wEx(X), X, 1) + betayEx(X));
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_42CC7FA8] ### Substitution of the known parameters in the analytical expression
wExSubs(X) = subs(wEx,{Lsym, psym, Gsym, Esym, Isym, Aqsym}, ...
    {XLx, propStr.pBar, propStr.G, propStr.E, YLy*(propStr.t^3)/12, ...
    propStr.alpha*YLy*propStr.t});
betayExSubs(X) = subs(betayEx, {Lsym, psym, Gsym, Esym, Isym, Aqsym}, ...
    {XLx, propStr.pBar, propStr.G, propStr.E, YLy*(propStr.t^3)/12, ...
    propStr.alpha*YLy*propStr.t});
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D4E5918D] ## Verification of the the accuracy of the page-wise implementation
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_98497D7F] ### **Quadrilateral mesh**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B0B09769] #### Choose number of elements in the mesh
%[text] Number of elements along the $X$-direction
numElx = 4;
%[text] Number of elements along the $Y$-direction
numEly = 2;
%[text] Total number of elements
numEl = numElx*numEly;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_FA5BE8CD] #### Mesh generation
[nodesX, nodesY] = generateQuadrilateralMesh(X0, XLx, Y0, YLy, numElx, numEly);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C8B5926E] #### Rendering the mesh non-uniform
%[text] Check the following checkbox to render the mesh non-uniform **Note** This only works for `numElx = 4` and `numEly = 2` with the given values
isMeshNonUniform = false; %[control:checkbox:50e4]{"position":[20,25]}
if isMeshNonUniform
    if numElx ~= 4 || numEly ~= 2
        error("Making the mesh non-uniform only works for numElx = 4 and numEly = 2")
    end
%[text] Displace node 2
    nodesY(2, 1) = nodesY(2, 1) + 0.08; % y
%[text] Displace node 5
    nodesX(2, 2) = nodesX(2, 2) + 0.08; % x
    nodesY(5, 1) = nodesY(5, 1) - 0.08; % y
%[text] Displace node 8
    nodesX(2, 3) = nodesX(2, 3) - 0.08; % x
    nodesY(8, 1) = nodesY(8, 1) + 0.08; % y
%[text] Displace node 11
    nodesX(2, 4) = nodesX(2, 4) + 0.08; % x
    nodesY(11, 1) = nodesY(11, 1) + 0.08; % x
%[text] Displace node 14
    nodesY(14, 1) = nodesY(14, 1) - 0.08; % x
%[text] 
end
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_4A4EF0A6] ### **Four-noded bilinear quadrilateral mesh**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_828BAEA7] #### Mesh generation
numNodesElQ1 = 4;
mshQ1 = generateBilinearQuadrilateralMesh ...
    (numElx, numEly, numEl, nodesX, nodesY, numNodesElQ1);
numNodesQ1 = height(mshQ1.nodes);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E4C0AE9E] #### Dirichlet boundary conditions for the mesh with the bilinear quadrilateral elements
[freeDOFsQ1, homDOFsQ1] = ...
    utilityFunctionsCantileverPlate.getFreeDOFsBilinearQuadrilateralMesh ...
    (numNodesQ1, numEly);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0A24F150] #### Mesh plot
numVertices = numel(mshQ1.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshQ1, numVertices, true); %[output:4cd97641]
hold on; %[output:4cd97641]
[xsQ1, ysQ1, zsQ1] = createSupports3D(mshQ1.nodes, homDOFsQ1);
for k = 1:length(xsQ1(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ1(k, :), ysQ1(k, :), zsQ1(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:4cd97641]
end
hold off; %[output:4cd97641]
axis equal; %[output:4cd97641]
xlabel("$x$", Interpreter="latex") %[output:4cd97641]
ylabel("$y$", Interpreter="latex") %[output:4cd97641]
zlabel("$z$", Interpreter="latex") %[output:4cd97641]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_4E93D9EB] ### **Nine-noded biquadratic quadrilateral mesh**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1AC37C56] #### Mesh generation
numNodesElQ2 = 9;
[mshQ2, ~] = generateBiquadraticQuadrilateralMesh ...
    (numElx, numEly, nodesX, nodesY, mshQ1, numNodesElQ1, numNodesElQ2);
numNodesQ2 = height(mshQ2.nodes);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_CC6D5D21] #### Dirichlet boundary conditions for the mesh with the biquadratic quadrilateral elements
[freeDOFsQ2, homDOFsQ2] = utilityFunctionsCantileverPlate.getFreeDOFsBiquadraticQuadrilateralMesh(numNodesQ1, numNodesQ2, numEly);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_A156E8F7] #### Mesh plot
numVertices = numel(mshQ1.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshQ2, numVertices, true); %[output:4d3b2113]
hold on; %[output:4d3b2113]
[xsQ2, ysQ2, zsQ2] = createSupports3D(mshQ2.nodes, homDOFsQ2);
for k = 1:length(xsQ2(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ2(k, :), ysQ2(k, :), zsQ2(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:4d3b2113]
end
hold off; %[output:4d3b2113]
axis equal; %[output:4d3b2113]
xlabel("x") %[output:4d3b2113]
ylabel("y") %[output:4d3b2113]
zlabel("z") %[output:4d3b2113]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_425C9F2F] ### Master stiffness matrix and consistent nodal force vector with and without the page-wise implementation
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1F81F98E] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1 = ...
    @computeElementStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate;
computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1 = ...
    @computeBilinearBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
[KQ1, FQ1] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate ...
    (mshQ1, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1, ...
    propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C5E5B9BA] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1 = ...
    @computeBilinearBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1 = 'undefined';
[KQ1PageWise, FQ1PageWise] = ...
    computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVctReissnerMindlinPlatePageWise ...
    (mshQ1, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1, ...
    propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C988A776] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2 = ...
    @computeElementStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate;
computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2 = ...
    @computeBiquadraticBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
[KQ2, FQ2] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate ...
    (mshQ2, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2, ...
    propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_35BF7F88] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2 = ...
    @computeBiquadraticBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2 = 'undefined';
[KQ2PageWise, FQ2PageWise] = ...
    computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVctReissnerMindlinPlatePageWise ...
    (mshQ2, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2, ...
    propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_588F8DA7] ### Solution of the discrete linear equation system
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_10FD1BAA] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
numDOFsQ1 = 2*numNodesQ1;
uQ1 = zeros(numDOFsQ1, 1);
uQ1(freeDOFsQ1, 1) = ...
    KQ1(freeDOFsQ1, freeDOFsQ1)\FQ1(freeDOFsQ1);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_481A9D1D] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
uQ1PageWise = zeros(numDOFsQ1, 1);
uQ1PageWise(freeDOFsQ1, 1) = ...
    KQ1PageWise(freeDOFsQ1, freeDOFsQ1)\FQ1PageWise(freeDOFsQ1);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_ED9BEC6B] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
numDOFsQ2 = 2*numNodesQ2;
uQ2 = zeros(numDOFsQ2, 1);
uQ2(freeDOFsQ2, 1) = ...
    KQ2(freeDOFsQ2, freeDOFsQ2)\FQ2(freeDOFsQ2);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_A7E4E8F4] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
uQ2PageWise = zeros(numDOFsQ2, 1);
uQ2PageWise(freeDOFsQ2, 1) = ...
    KQ2PageWise(freeDOFsQ2, freeDOFsQ2)\FQ2PageWise(freeDOFsQ2);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B5E2AA96] ### Postprocessing the discrete solutions in terms of the vertical displacement field 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1724BD64] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
mshCurrQ1 = mshQ1;
scaling = 1; %[control:slider:0214]{"position":[11,12]}
mshCurrQ1.nodes(:, 3) = mshCurrQ1.nodes(:, 3) + scaling*uQ1(1:3:end, 1);
numVertices = numel(mshQ1.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshCurrQ1, numVertices, false); %[output:05ad36e8]
hold on; %[output:05ad36e8]
fsurf(wExSubs, [X0 XLx Y0 YLy], FaceColor=[203 65 84]/255, FaceAlpha=0.5, ... %[output:05ad36e8]
    LineStyle="none"); %[output:05ad36e8]
[xsQ1, ysQ1, zsQ1] = createSupports3D(mshCurrQ1.nodes, homDOFsQ1);
for k = 1:length(xsQ1(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ1(k, :), ysQ1(k, :), zsQ1(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:05ad36e8]
end
hold off; %[output:05ad36e8]
axis equal; %[output:05ad36e8]
xlabel("$x$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:05ad36e8]
ylabel("$y$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:05ad36e8]
zlabel("$z$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:05ad36e8]
legend("FEM", "", "analytical", Location="best") %[output:05ad36e8]
title("Plate's deformation using Q1 elements") %[output:05ad36e8]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C7BBA9EC] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional bilinear four-noded finite elements
mshCurrQ1PageWise = mshQ1;
scaling = 1; %[control:slider:1a4a]{"position":[11,12]}
mshCurrQ1PageWise.nodes(:, 3) = mshCurrQ1PageWise.nodes(:, 3) + ...
    scaling*uQ1PageWise(1:3:end, 1);
numVertices = numel(mshQ1.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshCurrQ1PageWise, numVertices, false); %[output:09ce3908]
hold on; %[output:09ce3908]
fsurf(wExSubs, [X0 XLx Y0 YLy], FaceColor=[203 65 84]/255, FaceAlpha=0.5, ... %[output:09ce3908]
    LineStyle="none"); %[output:09ce3908]
[xsQ1, ysQ1, zsQ1] = createSupports3D(mshCurrQ1PageWise.nodes, homDOFsQ1);
for k = 1:length(xsQ1(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ1(k, :), ysQ1(k, :), zsQ1(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:09ce3908]
end
hold off; %[output:09ce3908]
axis equal; %[output:09ce3908]
xlabel("$x$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:09ce3908]
ylabel("$y$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:09ce3908]
zlabel("$z$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:09ce3908]
legend("FEM", "", "analytical", Location="best") %[output:09ce3908]
title(["Plate's deformation using Q1 elements", "and page-wise implementation"]) %[output:09ce3908]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1BB61317] #### Standard implementation for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
mshCurrQ2 = mshQ2;
scaling = 1; %[control:slider:0151]{"position":[11,12]}
mshCurrQ2.nodes(:, 3) = mshCurrQ2.nodes(:, 3) + ...
    scaling*uQ2(1:3:end, 1);
numVertices = numel(mshQ1.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshCurrQ2, numVertices, false); %[output:22903171]
hold on; %[output:22903171]
fsurf(wExSubs, [X0 XLx Y0 YLy], FaceColor=[203 65 84]/255, FaceAlpha=0.5, ... %[output:22903171]
    LineStyle="none"); %[output:22903171]
[xsQ2, ysQ2, zsQ2] = createSupports3D(mshCurrQ2.nodes, homDOFsQ1);
for k = 1:length(xsQ2(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ2(k, :), ysQ2(k, :), zsQ2(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:22903171]
end
hold off; %[output:22903171]
axis equal; %[output:22903171]
xlabel("$x$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:22903171]
ylabel("$y$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:22903171]
zlabel("$z$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:22903171]
legend("FEM", "", "analytical", Location="best") %[output:22903171]
title("Plate's deformation using Q2 elements") %[output:22903171]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_ECBD261B] #### Page-wise implementation using sparse matrices for the two-dimenstional biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
mshCurrQ2PageWise = mshQ2;
scaling = 1; %[control:slider:3cc7]{"position":[11,12]}
mshCurrQ2PageWise.nodes(:, 3) = mshCurrQ2PageWise.nodes(:, 3) + ...
    scaling*uQ2PageWise(1:3:end, 1);
numVertices = numel(mshQ2.nodes(:, 1));
plotMesh2d(mshCurrQ2PageWise, numVertices, false); %[output:4be1443a]
hold on; %[output:4be1443a]
fsurf(wExSubs, [X0 XLx Y0 YLy], FaceColor=[203 65 84]/255, FaceAlpha=0.5, ... %[output:4be1443a]
    LineStyle="none"); %[output:4be1443a]
[xsQ2, ysQ2, zsQ2] = createSupports3D(mshCurrQ2PageWise.nodes, homDOFsQ1);
for k = 1:length(xsQ2(:, 1))
    plot3(xsQ2(k, :), ysQ2(k, :), zsQ2(k, :), 'Linewidth', 2, 'Color', 'black'); %[output:4be1443a]
end
hold off; %[output:4be1443a]
axis equal; %[output:4be1443a]
xlabel("$x$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:4be1443a]
ylabel("$y$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:4be1443a]
zlabel("$z$", "Interpreter","latex") %[output:4be1443a]
legend("FEM", "", "analytical", Location="best") %[output:4be1443a]
title(["Plate's deformation using Q2 elements", "and page-wise implementation"]) %[output:4be1443a]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D4CFCD1D] ## Runtime performance using sparse matrices and page-wise implementation of the bilinear four-noded finite elements
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_6CEB6F4C] ### Initialize auxiliary variables
numRef = 50;
stp = 7;
runtimePerformanceQ1 = zeros(ceil(numRef/stp), 2);
numDOFsQ1 = zeros(ceil(numRef/stp), 1);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_59D283CD] ### Loop over all the refinement levels
for ii = 1:stp:numRef
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_32336458] #### Generation of the the finite element mesh
%[text] Number of elements along the $X$-direction
    numElxRef = 4*ii;
%[text] Number of elements along the $Y$-direction
    numElyRef = 1*ii;
%[text] Total number of elements
    numElQ1 = numElxRef*numElyRef; % total number of elements    
%[text] Mesh generation
    [nodesXRef, nodesYRef] = ...
        generateQuadrilateralMesh(X0, XLx, Y0, YLy, numElxRef, numElyRef);
    mshQ1Ref = generateBilinearQuadrilateralMesh ...
        (numElxRef, numElyRef, numElQ1, nodesXRef, nodesYRef, numNodesElQ1);
    numNodesQ1Ref = height(mshQ1Ref.nodes);
    numDOFsQ1(ceil(ii/stp), 1) = 3*numNodesQ1Ref;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_3C52AB9D] #### Definition of the Dirichlet boundary conditions
    [freeDOFsQ1Ref, ~] = ...
        utilityFunctionsCantileverPlate.getFreeDOFsBilinearQuadrilateralMesh ...
        (numNodesQ1Ref, numElyRef);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_FCCC526F] #### Solution of the discrete problem using the standard Finite Element implementation
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_65A02DDE] ... starting the timer
    tic;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8CE4850E] ... computing of the stiffness matrix and consistent nodal force vector for the one-dimensional two-noded linear mesh
    computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1 = ...
        @computeElementStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate;
    computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1 = ...
        @computeBilinearBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
    [K, F] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate ...
        (mshQ1Ref, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1, ...
        propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_5404BB62] ... solving the discrete linear equation system
    [~] = K(freeDOFsQ1Ref, freeDOFsQ1Ref)\F(freeDOFsQ1Ref);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8E98BAEF] ... stopping the timer
    runtimePerformanceQ1(ceil(ii/stp), 1) = toc;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_02283F3F] #### Solution of the discrete problem using the page-wise Finite Element implementation with sparse matrices
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D1E01B18] ... starting the timer
    tic;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_16B83382] ... computing of the stiffness matrix and consistent nodal force vector for the one-dimensional two-noded linear mesh
    computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1 = ...
        @computeBilinearBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
    computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1 = 'undefined';
    [K, F] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVctReissnerMindlinPlatePageWise ...
        (mshQ1Ref, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ1, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ1, ...
        propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0F0F778B] ... solving the discrete linear equation system
    [~] = K(freeDOFsQ1Ref, freeDOFsQ1Ref)\F(freeDOFsQ1Ref);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0DEE95E4] ... stopping the timer
    runtimePerformanceQ1(ceil(ii/stp), 2) = toc;
%[text] 
end
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0DA5D19D] ### Display of the runtime performance comparison between the standard and the page-wise implementation
loglog(numDOFsQ1, runtimePerformanceQ1, LineWidth=2); %[output:1bb3c0fa]
legend("standard", "page-wise", Location="best") %[output:1bb3c0fa]
grid on; %[output:1bb3c0fa]
xlabel("No. DOFs") %[output:1bb3c0fa]
ylabel("Runtime (s)") %[output:1bb3c0fa]
title(["Comparison of the runtime performance between the standard and the", ... %[output:group:6f4eccf6] %[output:1bb3c0fa]
    "page-wise implementation for the two-dimensional bilinear elements", ""]) %[output:group:6f4eccf6] %[output:1bb3c0fa]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E7E56C2F] ## Runtime performance using sparse matrices and page-wise implementation of the biquadratic nine-noded finite elements
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1E2EDEC2] ### Initialize auxiliary variables
numRef = 31;
stp = 5;
runtimePerformanceQ2 = zeros(ceil(numRef/stp), 2);
numDOFsQ2 = zeros(ceil(numRef/stp), 1);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_ED17BCF5] ### Loop over all the refinement levels
for ii = 1:stp:numRef
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_1F82CA3B] #### Generation of the the finite element mesh
%[text] Number of elements along the $X$-direction
    numElxRef = 4*ii;
%[text] Number of elements along the $Y$-direction
    numElyRef = 1*ii;
%[text] Total number of elements
    numElQ2 = numElxRef*numElyRef;
%[text] Mesh generation
    [nodesXRef, nodesYRef] = ...
        generateQuadrilateralMesh(X0, XLx, Y0, YLy, numElxRef, numElyRef);
    mshQ1Ref = generateBilinearQuadrilateralMesh ...
        (numElxRef, numElyRef, numElQ2, nodesXRef, nodesYRef, numNodesElQ1);
    numNodesQ1Ref = height(mshQ1Ref.nodes);
    [mshQ2Ref, ~] = generateBiquadraticQuadrilateralMesh ...
        (numElxRef, numElyRef, nodesXRef, nodesYRef, mshQ1Ref, numNodesElQ1, numNodesElQ2);
    numNodesQ2Ref = height(mshQ2Ref.nodes);
    numDOFsQ2(ceil(ii/stp), 1) = 3*numNodesQ2Ref;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0CA545FF] #### Definition of the Dirichlet boundary conditions
    [freeDOFsQ2Ref, ~] = ...
        utilityFunctionsCantileverPlate.getFreeDOFsBiquadraticQuadrilateralMesh ...
        (numNodesQ1Ref, numNodesQ2Ref, numElyRef);    
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_31D60D10] #### Solution of the discrete problem using the standard Finite Element implementation
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_65A02DDE] ... starting the timer
    tic;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8CE4850E] ... computing of the stiffness matrix and consistent nodal force vector for the one-dimensional two-noded linear mesh
    computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2 = ...
        @computeElementStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate;
    computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2 = ...
        @computeBiquadraticBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
    [K, F] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVectorReissnerMindlinPlate ...
        (mshQ2Ref, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2, ...
        propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_5404BB62] ... solving the discrete linear equation system
    [~] = K(freeDOFsQ2Ref, freeDOFsQ2Ref)\F(freeDOFsQ2Ref);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8E98BAEF] ... stopping the timer
    runtimePerformanceQ2(ceil(ii/stp), 1) = toc;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0500EEFD] #### Solution of the discrete problem using the page-wise Finite Element implementation with sparse matrices
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_D1E01B18] ... starting the timer
    tic;
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_16B83382] ... computing of the stiffness matrix and consistent nodal force vector for the one-dimensional two-noded linear mesh
    computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2 = ...
        @computeBiquadraticBasisFunctionsAndFirstDerivatives;
    computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2 = 'undefined';
    [K, F] = computeMasterStiffMatrixandForceVctReissnerMindlinPlatePageWise ...
        (mshQ2Ref, computeBasisFunctionsAndDerivsQ2, computeStiffMatrixandForceVectorQ2, ...
        propStr);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0F0F778B] ... solving the discrete linear equation system
    [~] = K(freeDOFsQ2Ref, freeDOFsQ2Ref)\F(freeDOFsQ2Ref);
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0DEE95E4] ... stopping the timer
    runtimePerformanceQ2(ceil(ii/stp), 2) = toc;
%[text] 
end
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_40E2D210] ### Display of the runtime performance comparison between the standard and the page-wise implementation
loglog(numDOFsQ2, runtimePerformanceQ2, LineWidth=2); %[output:68670666]
legend("standard", "page-wise", Location="best") %[output:68670666]
grid on; %[output:68670666]
xlabel("No. DOFs") %[output:68670666]
ylabel("Runtime (s)") %[output:68670666]
title(["Comparison of the runtime performance between the standard and the", ... %[output:group:2a8eeaa6] %[output:68670666]
    "page-wise implementation for the two-dimensional biquadratic elements", ""]) %[output:group:2a8eeaa6] %[output:68670666]
